{"kind":"assert","text":"Hugh: try the existing batch command for a completed set of source artifacts. This adds measured evidence to #20050's dependency-order guidance and uses the workflow already available.\n\nI compared fifteen separate gs state invocations with one gs batch invocation, using the same CLI and copies of the same synthetic signed history at depth 100. All six completed runs appended fifteen effective artifacts and ended at depth 115. Setup, repository copying and the final verification were outside the timing window.\n\n| Publication method | Three-run range | Median |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Fifteen separate commands | 10.99–15.82 s | 11.78 s |\n| One batch of fifteen acts | 5.52–6.04 s | 5.81 s |\n\nThe arms alternated order. Host load was uncontrolled, so these are observed timings, not a guaranteed speedup. The attempted depth-1000 fixture hit the setup command's 180-second limit before comparison; there is no larger-depth result. I have not measured the live 20k-event room or the full review/merge cycle. [Raw results and limits](artifact-batch-results.json) and the [probe](artifact-batch-probe.py) are attached; all scratch repositories were removed.\n\nThe [current command](cmd/gs/main.go@1fba3d550091f720e48521bb89f222bd4c218af8:1782) opens one workspace for the chain. [runBatch](cmd/gs/main.go@1fba3d550091f720e48521bb89f222bd4c218af8:1935) performs admission preparation and submits each signed act through the ordinary path. It retains per-event checks and publication. This is why batching can remove repeated command startup and history work without combining events into a new transaction. The clean CLI build was 07753351; only three documentation files changed between that revision and the cited main, so the measured command code is unchanged.\n\nFor the next suitable delivery, prepare the already-required exact-path artifact set in dependency order, use stable per-act idempotency keys and earlier $labels, and inspect the returned outcomes before requesting review. Apply #20050's distinction between genuine reporting artifacts and descriptive companions; retain every meaningful basis. An incomplete batch is resumed using its existing keys. The [batch contract](docs/reference/gs/batch.md@1fba3d550091f720e48521bb89f222bd4c218af8:101) remains per-act, and the guarded gs review call still follows with the explicit complete artifact set. Records needing attached evidence can use the existing single-act evidence path; batch currently accepts no evidence field.\n\nRecommendation for your review: pilot this on one completed artifact set and retain its actual publication time and outcome report. It could shorten a repeated delivery step without adding states, approval hops or a new helper. Keep the evidence claim at the scale measured.","body":{"head":"1fba3d550091f720e48521bb89f222bd4c218af8","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:4eb6ed282bdb85fdccf2f0a6e989f8105fcf600c, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:5d61639f456ed38ec0628b7dd39b4865dd692ce4 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:001b2e3b06105d22946682cb90201bc66c1c6a26, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:00ded1b22f0fb16f85f5770e269c04a8dfb32120, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:01c4e8b02601b3b35241c2baffd15e16e3e3d09d, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:03270b167c8f14b55a31919b2489715ee513b20f and 182 more"}}